 ("greek","leda","Leda","the queen of Sparta and the swan, the egg or eggs (Helen, the Dioscuri, Clytemnestra), the Nemesis alternative (the Cypria's egg from Nemesis, Leda as nurse), the Leda of the sculptures and of Leonardo, Michelangelo and Yeats"),
 ("greek","actaeon","Actaeon","the hunter who saw Artemis bathing and was turned into a stag and torn by his fifty hounds, the older reasons (courting Semele, boasting: Stesichorus, Euripides's Bacchae), Chiron's statue for the grieving hounds, Titian's two paintings, the Actaeon of Giordano Bruno's Eroici furori"),
 ("greek","pentheus","Pentheus","the king of Thebes who refused Dionysus, the spying in the tree, torn apart by his mother Agave and the maenads (the Bacchae), the head carried as a lion's, the cousin of the god, the Pentheus of the Roman sarcophagi and of the modern theatre"),
 ("greek","callisto","Callisto","the Arcadian companion of Artemis seduced by Zeus in Artemis's shape, the bear, the son Arcas who nearly killed her, the Great and Little Bear, Hera's request that they never bathe in Ocean, the Arcadian cult and the tomb, the Callisto of Ovid and of Titian"),
 ("greek","deianira","Deianira","the wife of Heracles won from Achelous, Nessus the centaur and the poisoned blood, the robe sent in jealousy of Iole, the pyre on Oeta and her suicide (Sophocles's Trachiniae), the Deianira of Ovid's Heroides"),
 ("greek","alcmene_and_amphitryon","Alcmene and Amphitryon","the mother of Heracles and the husband whose shape Zeus took for the triple night, the twins Heracles and Iphicles, the trial at Thebes, the shrine of Alcmene and the stone found in her coffin at Haliartus, Plautus's Amphitruo and the comic tradition to Molière, Kleist and Giraudoux"),
 ("greek","electra","Electra","the daughter who waited, the recognition at the tomb by the lock and the footprint, the urn, the matricide urged and done (Aeschylus's Choephori, Sophocles and Euripides against each other), the marriage to Pylades, Strauss and Hofmannsthal, Jung's complex, O'Neill's Mourning Becomes Electra"),
 ("greek","clytemnestra","Clytemnestra","the daughter of Tyndareus who killed Agamemnon in the bath with the net and the axe, the motives (Iphigenia, Cassandra, Aegisthus), the beacon speech, killed by her son, the ghost in the Eumenides, the Clytemnestra of Pindar's Pythian 11, the Mycenae 'tomb of Clytemnestra', the modern rehabilitations"),
 ("greek","andromache","Andromache","Hector's wife of the scene at the gate, the captive of Neoptolemus and the mother of Molossus, Hermione's jealousy (Euripides's Andromache), the marriage to Helenus and the little Troy at Buthrotum (Aeneid III), Racine, the Andromache of Baudelaire's Le Cygne"),
 ("greek","hecuba","Hecuba","the queen of Troy, the fifty children, the dream of the torch, Polyxena's sacrifice and Polydorus's body, the revenge on Polymestor and the blinding, the transformation into a dog and the Cynossema on the Hellespont, Euripides's Hecuba and Trojan Women, Hamlet's 'What's Hecuba to him'"),
 ("greek","polyxena","Polyxena","the Trojan princess sacrificed on Achilles's tomb by Neoptolemus, the love of Achilles for her (the Cypria and the late versions where it killed him), the Polyxena sarcophagus of Çanakkale (c. 500 BCE), Euripides's Hecuba, the Polyxena of the vase painters"),
 ("greek","penthesilea","Penthesilea","the Amazon queen who came to Troy after Hector's death, killed by Achilles who loved her as she died, Thersites mocked and killed, the Aethiopis, the Exekias amphora, Kleist's Penthesilea where she kills him, the Amazons as a class"),
 ("greek","memnon","Memnon","the Ethiopian king son of Eos, the killer of Antilochus, killed by Achilles, the immortality granted by Zeus to Eos's tears (the dew), the Aethiopis, the Colossi of Memnon at Thebes and the singing statue (the Roman tourists' graffiti, the earthquake of 27 BCE, the repair that silenced it), the Memnonides birds"),
 ("greek","sarpedon","Sarpedon","the Lycian king son of Zeus killed by Patroclus, Zeus's tears of blood and the body carried home by Sleep and Death (the Euphronios krater, returned to Italy 2008), the Lycian hero cult at Xanthos, the other Sarpedon brother of Minos, the Lycian dynasty's claim"),
 ("greek","laocoon","Laocoön","the Trojan priest who struck the horse and was killed with his sons by the two serpents from Tenedos (Aeneid II, the lost Laocoön of Sophocles, Arctinus's Iliupersis), the statue found in 1506 on the Esquiline and Michelangelo's presence, Lessing's Laokoon and the limits of painting and poetry, the arm restored"),
 ("greek","palamedes","Palamedes","the inventor of letters, dice and the lighthouse who exposed Odysseus's feigned madness, framed with Priam's gold and stoned (the Cypria, Gorgias's Defence, Euripides's lost play), the father Nauplius's revenge with the false beacons at Caphereus, the cult at Methymna"),
 ("greek","protesilaus_and_laodamia","Protesilaus and Laodamia","the first Greek to leap ashore at Troy and die, the wife who asked for three hours of his return and followed him (the wax image), the tomb at Elaeus with the elms that withered toward Troy (Philostratus's Heroicus, Pliny), the Persian looting of the tomb (Herodotus IX.116), Wordsworth's Laodamia"),
 ("greek","philomela_and_procne","Philomela and Procne","the Athenian sisters, Tereus's rape and the cut tongue, the tapestry, the son Itys served at the table, the flight as nightingale, swallow and hoopoe (Ovid VI, Sophocles's Tereus), the nightingale of the poets from Sappho to Eliot's Waste Land"),
 ("greek","ixion","Ixion","the first murderer of kin, purified by Zeus and then lusting after Hera, the cloud Nephele and the centaurs born of it, the burning wheel in Tartarus (Pindar's Pythian 2), the Ixion of Aeschylus's lost play, the wheel in the Sisyphus-Tantalus-Ixion set"),
 ("greek","seven_against_thebes","The Seven against Thebes","the expedition of Polynices with Adrastus, Tydeus, Capaneus, Amphiaraus, Hippomedon, Parthenopaeus (the lists vary), the gates and the pairs, Capaneus struck by lightning on the wall, the brothers' mutual killing, Aeschylus's play, the Thebaid of Statius, the Epigoni's return, the tombs of the Seven at Eleusis (Pausanias)"),
 ("greek","adrastus","Adrastus","the king of Argos who married his daughters to the lion and the boar (Polynices and Tydeus), the only survivor of the Seven saved by the horse Arion, the suppliant at Eleusis for the bodies (Euripides's Suppliants), the hero cult at Sicyon and Cleisthenes's transfer of it (Herodotus V.67), the Epigoni"),
 ("greek","rhadamanthus_and_aeacus","Rhadamanthus and Aeacus","the two judges of the dead beside Minos: Rhadamanthus the Cretan lawgiver in Elysium (Odyssey IV), Aeacus the just king of Aegina whose prayer ended the drought and whose ants became the Myrmidons, the keeper of the keys of Hades, the Aeacidae (Peleus, Achilles), Plato's Gorgias on the three judges, the Aeaceum on Aegina"),
 ("greek","heracles_labours","The Twelve Labours (the Heracles cycle as story)","the hero's story as distinct from his cult (pantheon/greek has the god): Alcmene and the snakes in the cradle, the madness and the murder of his children, the labours in their canonical order and the Peisander and Apollodorus lists, Omphale, Deianira and Nessus, the pyre on Oeta, the Heracles of Euripides and Sophocles, the metopes of Olympia, the Stoic and Cynic Heracles, Farnese Hercules"),
 # ---------------- ROMAN, second wave ----------------
 ("roman","lucretia","Lucretia","the wife of Collatinus raped by Sextus Tarquinius, the oath and the suicide, the expulsion of the kings and the Republic founded on her body (Livy I.57-60, Ovid's Fasti II), Augustine's question in the City of God I.19, Shakespeare's poem, the Lucretias of Titian, Rembrandt and Artemisia, the exemplum's modern critique"),
 ("roman","verginia","Verginia","the plebeian girl claimed as a slave by the decemvir Appius Claudius and killed by her father Verginius in the Forum with a butcher's knife, the fall of the decemvirs (Livy III.44-58), the doublet of Lucretia, the Virginia of Macaulay and of Webster"),
 ("roman","coriolanus","Coriolanus","the patrician who took Corioli, was exiled by the plebs, led the Volsci against Rome, and was turned back by his mother Veturia and wife Volumnia at the gates (Livy II.33-40, Plutarch), the death among the Volsci or in old age, the temple of Fortuna Muliebris, Shakespeare's play and Brecht's reworking"),
 ("roman","horatii_and_curiatii","The Horatii and Curiatii","the triple combat between Rome and Alba under Tullus Hostilius, the surviving Horatius who killed his sister for mourning a Curiatius, the trial and the tigillum sororium (Livy I.24-26), Dumézil's Horace et les Curiaces, David's Oath of the Horatii (1784) and the Revolution"),
 ("roman","tarpeia","Tarpeia","the Vestal who opened the citadel to the Sabines for what they wore on their left arms and was crushed under the shields (Livy I.11, Propertius IV.4), the Tarpeian Rock named for her, the traitor or the heroine (the Piso version), the relief on the Basilica Aemilia"),
 ("roman","marcus_curtius","Marcus Curtius","the knight who rode armed into the chasm in the Forum that would close only for Rome's greatest treasure (Livy VII.6), the Lacus Curtius and its relief, the alternative Mettius Curtius the Sabine, the exemplum of devotio"),
 ("roman","cumaean_sibyl","The Cumaean Sibyl","the prophetess of Apollo at Cumae who guided Aeneas to the underworld with the golden bough (Aeneid VI), the nine books offered to Tarquin and the three bought (the Sibylline Books and the decemviri), the thousand years and the wish to die (Petronius, Eliot's epigraph), the cave at Cumae found in 1932, Michelangelo's Sibyl, the Christian Sibyl of the Dies Irae"),
 ("roman","regulus","Marcus Atilius Regulus","the consul captured by Carthage who returned to Rome on parole to argue against the exchange and went back to torture and death (Horace Odes III.5, Cicero, Livy's Periochae), the historicity dispute (Polybius's silence), the exemplum of fides, the Regulus of Turner's painting"),
 # ---------------- CELTIC, second wave ----------------
 ("celtic","emer","Emer","the wife of Cú Chulainn won by riddles (Tochmarc Emire), the six gifts, the jealousy of Fand and the wife's speech, the lament over the body (the Serglige and the death tales), the Emer of Yeats's plays"),
 ("celtic","scathach","Scáthach","the warrior woman of Alba who trained Cú Chulainn at Dún Scáith on Skye, the gae bolga taught, her daughter Uathach, the rival Aífe and the son Connla, the woman as arms-teacher in the Ulster cycle"),
 ("celtic","ferdiad","Ferdiad","Cú Chulainn's foster-brother trained beside him by Scáthach, bought by Medb with Finnabair, the three-day combat at the ford and the gae bolga through the horn skin, the lament (the Comrac Fir Diad), Ardee named for the ford"),
 ("celtic","conchobar","Conchobar mac Nessa","the king of Ulster born on the day Christ was born (the synchronism), Ness's bargain for the year of kingship, Deirdre and the betrayal of the sons of Uisliu, the brain-ball of Mesgegra lodged in his head and the death at the news of the Crucifixion, the Emain Macha court"),
 ("celtic","etain","Étaín","the woman of the Tochmarc Étaíne: the wife of Midir turned into a fly by Fuamnach, swallowed and reborn, the wife of Eochaid, won back by Midir at fidchell and flying away as swans, the Sídhe of Brí Léith, the Étaín of the Yeats and Moore reworkings"),
 ("celtic","pwyll_and_pryderi","Pwyll and Pryderi","the prince of Dyfed who exchanged places with Arawn and won Rhiannon, the son who vanished at birth and was found with the foal, the Three Branches' Pryderi (the enchantment of Dyfed, the pigs of Annwn, killed by Gwydion in single combat), the only figure in all four branches"),
 ("celtic","peredur","Peredur","the Welsh Perceval of Peredur fab Efrawg: the boy raised in the forest without arms, Arthur's court, the head on the platter and the bleeding lance (the Grail without the Grail), the Empress of Constantinople, the relation to Chrétien's Perceval debated"),
 ("celtic","owain","Owain (Yvain)","the historical Owain mab Urien of Rheged made romance hero: the Lady of the Fountain, the lion, the ravens of the Dream of Rhonabwy, Chrétien's Yvain and the Welsh Owain, Taliesin's elegy for the historical prince"),
 # ---------------- NORSE, second wave ----------------
 ("norse","gudrun_kriemhild","Gudrun (Kriemhild)","Sigurd's widow: the potion of forgetting, the marriage to Atli and the revenge on her brothers by killing her own sons and serving them (the Atlakvida and Atlamál), against the Nibelungenlied's Kriemhild who avenges Siegfried on her brothers and dies by Hildebrand's sword, the two traditions' inversion, Wagner's Gutrune"),
 ("norse","sigmund","Sigmund","the Volsung who drew Odin's sword from the tree Barnstokk, the wolf-skin years with his son Sinfjotli, the revenge on Siggeir, the death in battle when Odin broke the sword, the father of Sigurd, the Beowulf digression on Sigemund the dragon-slayer (the older form)"),
 ("norse","signy","Signy","the Volsung sister married to Siggeir who bore a son by her own brother Sigmund in a witch's shape to breed an avenger (Sinfjotli), the burning hall and her choice to die in it (Volsunga saga), the Signy of Ibsen and the Scandinavian revival"),
 ("norse","aslaug","Aslaug (Kráka)","the daughter of Sigurd and Brynhild hidden in a harp by Heimir, the peasant's foster-child who answered Ragnar's riddle (neither dressed nor undressed), the wife of Ragnar and mother of Ivar, the Aslaug of the TV series as reception"),
 ("norse","lagertha","Lagertha","the shieldmaiden of Saxo's Gesta Danorum (IX) who fought with her hair loose, married Ragnar and later killed her second husband with a spearhead hidden in her gown, the Norse origin question (Thorgerd), the Lagertha of the Vikings series"),
 ("norse","hrolf_kraki","Hrolf Kraki","the Danish king of Lejre, the nephew of Helgi, the champions (Bodvar Bjarki, Hjalti), the visit to Adils at Uppsala and the gold scattered on the Fyrisvellir, the death in the burning hall by Skuld's sorcery, the Hrothulf of Beowulf, the Hrólfs saga kraka and the Bjarkamál"),
 ("norse","bodvar_bjarki","Bödvar Bjarki","the champion born of a bear-cursed father, the bear that fought while he sat in trance, the making of Hott into Hjalti with the dragon's blood, the death at Lejre, the Beowulf parallel (Panzer's Bear's Son) and its critics"),
 ("norse","atli_etzel","Atli (Etzel, the Attila of legend)","Attila the Hun as the Edda's greedy Atli killed by Gudrun and the Nibelungenlied's gracious Etzel at whose court the Burgundians die, the Atlakvida's gold and the snake pit, the historical death of 453 and the bride Ildico as the seed of the legend, the Thidrekssaga"),
 # ---------------- SLAVIC, second wave ----------------
 ("slavic","vasilisa","Vasilisa the Beautiful","the girl with the doll from her dead mother sent to Baba Yaga for fire, the skull-lantern that burned the stepmother, the shirts for the tsar, Afanasyev's tale, the Vasilisa the Wise of the Frog Princess, Propp's analysis, Bilibin's illustrations"),
 ("slavic","ivan_tsarevich","Ivan Tsarevich","the third son of the Russian tales: the Firebird and the grey wolf, the Frog Princess, Koschei's death in the egg, the brothers who killed him and the water of life, the archetype (Propp's Morphology), Stravinsky and Bilibin"),
 ("slavic","marya_morevna","Marya Morevna","the warrior princess who kept Koschei chained in her closet, Ivan's disobedience and the three lives, the horses of Baba Yaga, the tale in Afanasyev, the amazon of the Russian tradition"),
 ("slavic","mikula_selyaninovich","Mikula Selyaninovich","the ploughman bogatyr whose plough Volga's druzhina could not lift, the peasant stronger than the prince and the giant, the earth's own strength (Svyatogor's bag), the byliny of Volga and Mikula"),
 ("slavic","libuse","Libuše","the prophetess princess who founded Prague ('a city whose glory will touch the stars'), the judgment scorned and the choice of the ploughman Přemysl as husband, Cosmas of Prague's Chronica Boemorum (12th c.), the Maidens' War of Vlasta after her death, Smetana's opera, the Czech national myth"),
 ("slavic","marko_kraljevic","Marko Kraljević","the Serbian prince (d. 1395, an Ottoman vassal) made the great hero of the South Slavic epic: the horse Šarac, the wine, the fights with the Arabs and the Turks, the mother Jevrosima, the death and the sleeping-hero cave, Vuk Karadžić's collection, the Bulgarian and Macedonian Marko, the Yugoslav uses"),
 ("slavic","lech_czech_and_rus","Lech, Czech and Rus","the three brothers who founded the Polish, Czech and Russian nations, the white eagle's nest at Gniezno, the Wielkopolska Chronicle (14th c.) and the Dalimil Chronicle, the invented tradition and its modern uses, the Krak and Wanda legends of Kraków as the companion (the dragon of Wawel, the princess who drowned rather than marry the German)"),
 ("slavic","krak_and_wanda","Krak and Wanda","the founder of Kraków who killed (or whose sons killed, or the cobbler Skuba killed) the Wawel dragon with the sulphur-stuffed sheep, the Krakus Mound, the daughter Wanda who threw herself into the Vistula rather than marry the German prince, Kadłubek's chronicle (c. 1200), the Wanda Mound, the Polish national school versions"),
 # ---------------- IBERIAN ----------------
 ("iberian","el_cid","El Cid (Rodrigo Díaz de Vivar)","the Castilian knight of the Cantar (c. 1200): the exile, the daughters and the Infantes de Carrión, the beard, Valencia, Babieca and Tizona, the dead Cid riding out (the Crónica particular), the historical Rodrigo who served the Muslim king of Zaragoza (the Historia Roderici), Corneille's Le Cid, the 1961 film, Franco's Cid, the tomb at Burgos"),
 ("iberian","roland_at_roncevaux","Roland and Roncevaux","the Frankish count of the Breton march killed in the Pyrenean pass in 778 (Einhard's one line), the Chanson de Roland (the Oxford manuscript, c. 1100): Ganelon, the horn, Durendal, the death facing Spain, the Basque ambushers made Saracens, the Nota Emilianense and the Spanish tradition, Bernardo del Carpio as the Spanish counter-hero, the Orlando of Boiardo and Ariosto, the Roland statues of the Hanseatic towns"),
 ("iberian","bernardo_del_carpio","Bernardo del Carpio","the Leonese hero invented against Roland: the nephew of Alfonso the Chaste born of a secret marriage, the father imprisoned, the victory at Roncevaux over Charlemagne in the Spanish version, the romances and the Poema (lost), the Bernardo of Lope de Vega and of the Spanish nationalism"),
 ("iberian","don_rodrigo_and_la_cava","Don Rodrigo and La Cava","the last Visigothic king who opened the locked tower of Toledo and raped (or seduced) Florinda la Cava, daughter of Count Julian, whose revenge brought the Moors in 711, the battle of Guadalete, the penitent king in the tomb with the snake (the romances), the Arabic sources (al-Maqqari), the myth of the loss of Spain and its uses (Menéndez Pidal's study, Landor, Scott, Southey)"),
 ("iberian","seven_infantes_of_lara","The Seven Infantes of Lara","the seven sons of Gonzalo Gustioz betrayed by their uncle Ruy Velázquez and his wife Doña Lambra, the heads brought to the father imprisoned at Córdoba, the half-brother Mudarra born of a Moorish woman who avenged them, the lost epic reconstructed by Menéndez Pidal from the chronicles and the romances, the Salas de los Infantes"),
 ("iberian","pelayo","Pelayo","the Visigothic noble who defeated the Moors at Covadonga (c. 722) and founded the kingdom of Asturias, the cave and the Virgin, the Crónica de Alfonso III's account and the Arabic silence, the Reconquista's founding myth, the Covadonga of the Carlists and of Franco, the tomb in the Santa Cueva"),
 ("iberian","jaun_zuria","Jaun Zuria","the White Lord, the first Lord of Biscay of the Basque legend: the son of a Scottish (or Basque) princess and Sugaar the serpent, the victory at Padura (Arrigorriaga, the red stones) over the Leonese, García de Salazar's 15th-century account, the Basque nationalist uses (Sabino Arana) and the Bizkaia foral myth"),
 ("iberian","fernan_gonzalez","Fernán González","the first count of independent Castile (10th c.) made epic hero: the Poema de Fernán González (c. 1250, Arlanza), the horse and the hawk sold to the king for a debt that grew until Castile was free, the battles of Hacinas and Lara, the imprisonment and the rescue by the Navarrese princess Sancha, the Arlanza monastery's promotion of the legend"),
 # ---------------- MEDIEVAL ----------------
 ("medieval","wilhelm_tell","Wilhelm Tell","the crossbowman of Uri who shot the apple from his son's head at Gessler's order and killed the bailiff in the Hohle Gasse (the White Book of Sarnen c. 1470, Tschudi), the Palnatoki of Saxo as the Danish source of the apple-shot, the 1291 oath and the Rütli, the historicity demolished (Kopp 1835) and the Swiss myth kept, Schiller's play and Rossini's opera"),
 ("medieval","tristan_and_isolde","Tristan and Isolde","the Cornish knight and the Irish princess, the love potion on the ship, the tryst under the tree, the leap from the chapel, the black and white sails (Thomas, Béroul, Eilhart, Gottfried's unfinished masterpiece, the Prose Tristan and Malory), the Drustanus stone at Fowey and the Pictish Drust, the Diarmuid and Gráinne parallel, Wagner's Tristan (1865)"),
 ("medieval","parzival","Parzival (Perceval)","the boy raised in ignorance by his mother in the forest, the red knight, the Grail castle and the unasked question, the years of wandering, the hermit's teaching and the return, Chrétien's unfinished Perceval and the Continuations, Wolfram's Parzival with Kyot and the stone Grail, the Welsh Peredur (celtic/), Wagner's Parsifal, the Grail scholarship (Loomis, the 'Celtic origins' debate)"),
 ("medieval","tannhauser","Tannhäuser","the historical Minnesänger (13th c.) made the knight who lived in the Venusberg, went to Rome for absolution and was refused ('when this staff blooms'), the staff that bloomed three days after he had gone back to Venus, the ballad of the 15th century, Heine's poem, Wagner's opera and the Paris scandal of 1861, the Hörselberg"),
 ("medieval","faust","Faust","the historical Georg (or Johann) Faust of the 1500s (the Trithemius letter, the Wittenberg records, the death at Staufen c. 1540), the Faustbuch of 1587, Marlowe's Doctor Faustus, the puppet plays, Goethe's two parts (1808, 1832), the pact and the Mephistopheles of the pantheon (pantheon/abrahamic has him), Mann's Doktor Faustus, Bulgakov, the Faustian bargain as the modern phrase"),
 ("medieval","till_eulenspiegel","Till Eulenspiegel","the trickster of the 1515 Strasbourg chapbook (Hermann Bote of Brunswick as probable compiler), the ninety-five tales of literal-minded mischief, the Mölln grave of 1350 and the historical question, the Flemish Uilenspiegel of De Coster's 1867 novel as a Protestant rebel, Strauss's tone poem"),
 ("medieval","pied_piper","The Pied Piper of Hamelin","the 1284 loss of 130 children of Hamelin recorded in the town's window (c. 1300) and the Lüneburg manuscript (c. 1440), the rats added in the 16th century, the theories (emigration to the east, the children's crusade, the dancing mania, a plague), Grimm's Deutsche Sagen, Browning's poem, the Bungelosenstrasse where no music is played"),
 ("medieval","lohengrin","Lohengrin","the Swan Knight who came to Brabant to defend Elsa on the condition she never ask his name, the question asked and the departure, Wolfram's epilogue and the Middle High German Lohengrin (c. 1290), the Chevalier au Cygne of the Crusade cycle and the Godfrey of Bouillon lineage, Wagner's opera (1850) and Ludwig II's Neuschwanstein"),
 ("medieval","robin_hood","Robin Hood","the outlaw of Sherwood or Barnsdale: the ballads (Robin Hood and the Monk c. 1450, the Gest c. 1500), Little John, Will Scarlet, Friar Tuck and Maid Marian as accretions, the Sheriff and the king, the death at Kirklees by the prioress's bleeding, the candidates (Robert Hod of 1225, the Wakefield Robin), Holt's and Knight's studies, the May games, the modern Robin who robs the rich (a late turn: say so)"),
 # ---------------- EGYPTIAN (the tales) ----------------
 ("egyptian","sinuhe","Sinuhe","the courtier who fled Egypt at Amenemhat I's death, the years in Retjenu, the duel with the champion, the letter of Senusret I and the return to die in Egypt (the Middle Kingdom's masterpiece, Berlin Papyrus 3022, the Ashmolean ostracon), Parkinson's edition, Waltari's Sinuhe the Egyptian (1945) and the film"),
 ("egyptian","shipwrecked_sailor","The Shipwrecked Sailor","the tale of the sailor cast on the island of the Ka and the great serpent with the golden body who foretold his rescue and gave him gifts, the island that vanished (Papyrus Leningrad 1115, Middle Kingdom), the oldest sea-marvel tale and its comparanda (Sinbad, Odysseus)"),
 ("egyptian","setne_khamwas","Setne Khamwas (Khaemwaset)","the fourth son of Ramesses II, high priest of Ptah and restorer of the pyramids (the 'first Egyptologist'), made hero of the demotic tales: the Book of Thoth taken from the tomb of Naneferkaptah and the ghost's story, the seductress Tabubu, the descent to the underworld with his son Si-Osire (the Setne cycle, Ptolemaic-Roman papyri), the tomb in the Serapeum question"),
 ("egyptian","djedi","Djedi the magician","the magician of the Westcar Papyrus who rejoined a severed goose's head and knew the number of the secret chambers of Thoth, summoned to Khufu's court, the prophecy of the three kings born of Ruddedet (the Fifth Dynasty's origin), the Khufu of the tale against the pyramid builder"),
 ("egyptian","wenamun","Wenamun","the priest of Amun sent to Byblos for cedar (c. 1075 BCE) in the Report of Wenamun (Papyrus Pushkin 120): the theft at Dor, the prince of Byblos's contempt, the ecstatic youth, the storm to Alashiya, the tale as literature or report (the debate), the evidence for the collapse of Egyptian power"),
 ("egyptian","two_brothers","The Two Brothers (Anpu and Bata)","the tale of Papyrus d'Orbiney (19th Dynasty): the wife's false accusation, Bata's self-castration and the heart in the cedar flower, the bull and the persea trees, the rebirth as king, the folktale type (the Potiphar's-wife motif and Joseph, the tale of the two brothers across Eurasia), the gods Anubis and Bata as the brothers' names"),
 ("egyptian","rhampsinitus_thief","The Thief of Rhampsinitus","Herodotus II.121: the master builder's sons who robbed the king's treasury through the hidden stone, the brother beheaded, the corpse guarded and stolen with wine, the princess and the dead man's arm, the pardon and the marriage, the oldest recorded trickster tale of Egypt and its folk parallels"),
 ("egyptian","nitocris","Nitocris (the legend)","the queen of Herodotus II.100 who avenged her brother by drowning his murderers in an underground chamber and threw herself into the ashes, Manetho's Nitocris 'the bravest and most beautiful, with a rosy complexion' who built the third pyramid, the Sixth Dynasty king Neitiqerty as the name's origin (Ryholt), the Babylonian Nitocris of Herodotus I as a different figure, Lovecraft's Nitocris"),
 # ---------------- MESOPOTAMIAN, second wave ----------------
 ("mesopotamian","enmerkar","Enmerkar","the king of Uruk who invented writing to threaten the lord of Aratta (Enmerkar and the Lord of Aratta), the contests of riddles and the goddess Inanna between them, Enmerkar and En-suhgir-ana, the Sumerian King List's founder of Uruk, the Nimrod identification of the scholars"),
